  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user confirming an action (deleting a message, alerting the moderators, reverting an icon, refusing the MP storage), I want the alert's buttons to name what they do, so that I cannot confirm an irreversible action by reading only « Oui ».\n\n### Rule\n\n\"Create succinct, logical button titles. Aim for a one- or two-word title that describes the result of selecting the button. Prefer verbs and verb phrases that relate directly to the alert text […] In informational alerts only, you can use \"OK\" for acceptance, avoiding \"Yes\" and \"No.\" Always use \"Cancel\" to title a button that cancels the alert's action.\" and \"A specific button title like \"Erase,\" \"Convert,\" \"Clear,\" or \"Delete\" helps people understand the action they're taking.\" — [HIG › Alerts](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/alerts) (Buttons; page updated 2024-02-02).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n| Alert | Buttons | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| « Supprimer ce message ? » (irreversible) | « Non » (cancel) / « Oui » (destructive) | `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Actions/ReaderEditFlow.swift:32-33` |\n| « Alerter les modérateurs par email ? » | « Non » / « Oui » | `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Actions/ReaderAlertFlow.swift:26-27` |\n| « Revenir à l'icône précédente ? » | « Oui » / « Garder » (cancel) | `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/AppIconSeasonModel.swift:125-126` |\n| « Sans stockage MP » | « Confirmer » (destructive) / « Revenir » (cancel) | `App/SwiftHFR/MPStorage/MPStorageCreationQuestionView.swift:33-35` |\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\n- The first two alerts are identical: `HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift:5521-5523` and `:5534-5536` (« Non » / « Oui »).\n- The icon question and the MP storage sheet have no counterpart (legacy's MP storage question is one OK / Cancel alert, `Classes/MPStorage.m:91`); the current MP storage form is an operator decision (#1014).\n\n### Class\n\n**(b) evolution, M5** for the two reader alerts (same as legacy, wording only). The two SwiftHFR-only alerts have no parity to keep and can take the same pass.\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- « Supprimer » (destructive) / « Annuler »; « Préparer l'email » / « Annuler »; « Revenir » / « Garder »; « Ne pas créer » / « Annuler ». Roles unchanged.\n- Check: a test on each alert's button titles; no rendering needed.\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
